<title>USA: Fed may up rates, but Greenspan is key--Fed alumni.</title>
<headline>Fed may up rates, but Greenspan is key--Fed alumni.</headline>
<byline>Jose Paulo Vicente</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. economy is healthy, labor markets are tight, consumer spending is showing incipient signs of waning and inflation remains a missing person; you are dazed with mixed signals but still have to decide on whether to raise interest rates.</p>
<p>So who are you going to call?</p>
<p>Alan Greenspan, the Chairman of the Federal Reserve.</p>
</text>
